#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283253 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "812bd6b3-17b1-527d-8b58-b77ec93b1871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283255}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "812bd6b3-17b1-527d-8b58-b77ec93b1871" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283255} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f103862-4811-51d6-85cd-845062526155" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e4819488-a7a0-5944-ad18-73e05d2e8341" :question/math-academy-id "q-281581" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=3$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=21.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=3$ passes through the points $P(0,3)$ and $Q(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 10 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(9,3)$ and ${Q}^{′}(10,1).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1-3}{10-9}(x-9) \\\\ y-3 & =-2(x-9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =-2x+18 \\\\ 2x+y & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15e8730b-c59a-5897-8c83-073b54f517a9" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Standard Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3f57e7e-1a4e-506c-8c8f-f93617e872c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280954} {:answer/id #uuid "730fcfe2-2009-559c-bcd5-59d421a033b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280955}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "730fcfe2-2009-559c-bcd5-59d421a033b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x-7y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280955} :answer-field/id #uuid "48df28e7-8f48-5d7a-9e4d-34bfe8c30265" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "534b0fc4-23b0-567d-ab9e-8474a8eb5bc9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281586" :question/problem "Consider the line $-4x+y+1=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **standard form**, the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T$ is\n\n{{field-1}}$=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $-4x+y+1=0$ passes through the points $P(0,-1)$ and $Q(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $P$ and $Q$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${P}^{′}(-1,-2)$ and ${Q}^{′}(6,6).$\n\nNow, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${P}^{′}$ and ${Q}^{′}$ in point-slope form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y+2 & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{6-(-1)}(x+1) \\\\ y+2 & =\\frac{8}{7}(x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we transform the equation of the line to standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7y+14 & =8x+8 \\\\ 8x-7y & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n8x-7y=6\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290319 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c8f0fa1-a86a-577f-bdc9-fc7427faa18d" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Image of a Line Given by an Equation in Slope-Intercept Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08fd19ea-c633-517a-b1c9-ee6f8212d9fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13x+3y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290321} {:answer/id #uuid "613759be-094a-5654-974d-97ea77254189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+3y+12=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290322} {:answer/id #uuid "b842027f-3e17-54b4-a2d1-ffe6e2b3cf0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+13y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290323} {:answer/id #uuid "73f7fd2a-8954-5b8d-92f4-2fbd1546f8b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13x+8y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290324} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e4427b-7761-5a55-b634-a5cadfd2e927" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+3y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b842027f-3e17-54b4-a2d1-ffe6e2b3cf0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8x+13y+2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290323} :answer-field/id #uuid "625f4560-f4c4-52df-8e53-891c0a200f7d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290320}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a72a83e-c00c-5e25-8dc9-1f34b89688c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77776" :question/problem "Consider the line $y=4x-1$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the line $y=4x-1$ passes through the points $Q(0,-1)$ and $R(1,3)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $Q$ and $R$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -10 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${Q}^{′}(3,-2)$ and ${R}^{′}(-10,6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${Q}^{′}$ and ${R}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-2) & =\\frac{6-(-2)}{-10-3}(x-3) \\\\ y+2 & =-\\frac{8}{13}(x-3) \\\\ 13y+26 & =-8x+24 \\\\ 8x+13y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
